---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '@/components/primitives/Section.astro';
import Prose from '@/components/primitives/Prose.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '@/components/primitives/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site.config';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Terms', href: '/terms' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  titleFull="Terms of service | Murikah"
  description="The terms that govern use of Murikah websites and online services, including Murikah Tutor."
>
  <Section tone="surface" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} class="mb-6" />
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1
      id="page-title"
      class="mt-5 font-serif text-[length:var(--text-title)] leading-[1.06] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-navy"
    >
      Terms of service
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Last updated: 21 September 2026</p>

    <Prose class="mt-10">
      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of murikah.com and online services that
        link to these Terms, including Murikah Tutor at tutor.murikah.com. By accessing or using a
        covered service, you agree to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>1. About Murikah</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah provides assurance, governance, software, learning and related digital services.
        Questions about these Terms can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You must provide accurate information when creating or using an account and keep your
        authentication credentials secure. You are responsible for activity carried out through your
        account unless the activity results from a security failure for which you are not responsible.
      </p>
      <p>
        Murikah Tutor may offer limited guest use before requiring an account. Guest limits, feature
        limits and availability may change over time. A guest conversation may be preserved and
        associated with your account when you sign up or sign in.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you use Google or another supported identity provider to sign in, you also remain subject
        to that provider's applicable terms. Using single sign-on does not give Murikah access to
        unrelated content in your Google or other provider account.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may use Murikah services only for lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to accounts, systems, data or infrastructure;</li>
        <li>interfere with, overload, probe or disrupt the service or its security controls;</li>
        <li>use automated means to circumvent quotas, guest limits or access restrictions;</li>
        <li>upload or distribute malware, malicious code or content that unlawfully infringes rights;</li>
        <li>impersonate another person or misrepresent your authority to act for an organisation;</li>
        <li>
          use the service to violate applicable law, privacy rights, intellectual-property rights or
          contractual obligations; or
        </li>
        <li>
          use Murikah services in a way that creates a material risk to other users, our systems or
          third parties.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. AI-assisted features</h2>
      <p>
        Some Murikah services use artificial intelligence and automated tools. AI-generated content
        can be incomplete, inaccurate, outdated or unsuitable for your circumstances. You are
        responsible for reviewing important outputs before relying on them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unless Murikah expressly agrees otherwise in writing, Tutor output is for learning,
        drafting, research support and general informational use. It is not a substitute for legal,
        medical, financial, tax, audit or other regulated professional advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not rely on AI-generated output alone for decisions that could materially affect a
        person's rights, safety, employment, finances, education, health or legal position.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of content you submit to Murikah to the extent you own it. You give us
        a limited licence to host, copy, transmit, transform and process that content only as
        reasonably necessary to operate, secure and provide the service, comply with law and support
        features you request.
      </p>
      <p>
        You must have the rights and permissions needed to submit the content you provide. Do not
        upload confidential, personal or regulated information unless you are authorised to do so
        and the service is appropriate for that information.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Generated outputs</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to applicable law and third-party rights, you may use outputs generated for you by
        Murikah services. Because AI systems can produce similar material for different users, we do
        not promise that generated output will be unique or that it will not resemble content
        produced for someone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for checking whether an output is suitable for your intended use and
        whether attribution, permission, licensing or other review is required.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Murikah intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah and its licensors retain all rights in the services, software, designs, trademarks,
        documentation, templates and other materials that we provide, excluding your content and
        rights that cannot lawfully be claimed by us.
      </p>
      <p>
        These Terms do not grant you a right to copy, resell, reverse engineer or commercially
        exploit the Murikah service itself except where applicable law expressly permits it or we
        agree in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah relies on third-party infrastructure, authentication, AI, search, communications and
        other service providers. Their services may be subject to separate terms and availability.
        We are not responsible for third-party services that you access independently of Murikah,
        but we remain responsible for our own obligations when we choose processors to support the
        service.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we collect, use, store and share
        personal data. It forms an important part of the service relationship and includes specific
        information about Murikah Tutor, guest use and Google Sign-In.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Service availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep Murikah services reliable, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or
        error-free operation. Features may depend on third-party providers, Internet connectivity
        and maintenance windows.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may add, change, suspend or retire features where reasonably necessary for security,
        performance, legal, commercial or product reasons. Where a change materially affects a paid
        service, any specific customer agreement takes priority over these general Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Fees and paid services</h2>
      <p>
        Some Murikah services may be free, limited, trial-based or paid. Any applicable price,
        billing period, taxes and material payment terms will be shown or agreed before you are
        charged. Separate proposals, statements of work, subscriptions or customer agreements may
        contain additional commercial terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the service at any time. Where account controls are available, you may
        sign out or request account/data action through the contact details in our Privacy Policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may restrict or suspend access where reasonably necessary to address security risks,
        unlawful use, material breach of these Terms, non-payment for a paid service or serious risk
        to other users or the service. Where practical, we will act proportionately to the issue.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, Murikah services are provided on an "as available" basis.
        We do not guarantee that every output, recommendation, search result, generated diagram or
        other result will be accurate, complete, suitable or available at all times.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these Terms excludes any guarantee, duty or remedy that cannot lawfully be
        excluded under applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, Murikah will not be liable for indirect, incidental,
        consequential, special or punitive loss arising solely from use of a free or general
        informational service, including loss of profits, revenue, goodwill or opportunity.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a paid engagement or subscription, any specific written agreement with Murikah may set
        different liability terms and will prevail to the extent of a conflict with these general
        Terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not exclude or limit liability where doing so would be unlawful, including liability
        that cannot legally be excluded for fraud or other non-excludable obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of Kenya, unless mandatory law in your location
        requires otherwise. We encourage you to contact us first so that we can try to resolve a
        dispute promptly. Subject to applicable mandatory rights, the courts of Kenya will have
        jurisdiction over disputes arising from these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms as our services or legal obligations change. The current version
        will be published on this page with the updated date. If a material change requires
        additional notice or consent, we will provide it where appropriate.
      </p>

      <h2>17. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
